// A record-level validation rule (spec §6.1): a booking must end after it
// starts, and must not overlap another booking of the same room.
//
//   minab run examples/booking-overlap.minab
//   minab run examples/booking-overlap.minab --trace
//
// The local half (`.end_date > .start_date`) is answered from the record
// in the config; only the correlated half reaches the database, as one
// parameterized EXISTS.

.end_date > .start_date AND NOT EXISTS(
    #Booking[. != ^ AND .room_id == ^.room_id
             AND .start_date < ^.end_date AND .end_date > ^.start_date]
)
